<title>SWEDEN: Trygg-Hansa starts employee share options.</title>
<headline>Trygg-Hansa starts employee share options.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish insurance company Trygg-Hansa AB said on Wednesday it was extending its employee bonus program to include five-year stock options.</p>
<p>&quot;The options' value will be affected by the stock's price performance, thereby establishing a clear connection between the employees' and shareholders' long-term interests,&quot; Trygg-Hansa said in a statement.</p>
<p>At first the programme will include around 100 key employees in the group, Trygg-Hansa said.</p>
<p>&quot;The options entitle its owners to purchase existing shares and thus do not entail any dilution for the existing shareholders,&quot; Trygg-Hansa said.</p>
<p>Nor would the option programme affect the company's costs, it said.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
